  "severity": "important",
  "description": "A flaw was found in util-linux's nsenter. The --join-cgroup option opens the target cgroup.procs file as root and keeps the file descriptor open across later credential changes and execve(). If a privileged user runs nsenter --join-cgroup against an attacker-controlled target, a program run there can inherit root's ability to move, and then terminate, unrelated host processes.",
